<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/6th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Gwansanseong</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/554">554</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Gwansanseong was fought in 554 at the fortress of Gwansanseong, near modern Okcheon in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>, between Baekje and Silla. King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seong-of-baekje">Seong of Baekje</a> attacked Silla in revenge for its seizure of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-river">Han River</a> basin, but was killed and his army destroyed; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samguk-sagi">Samguk sagi</a> reports nearly 30,000 Baekje dead. The defeat ended the Baekje–Silla alliance and left Silla in control of the Han basin.</p></div>
